cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Normalizing abbreviated French clinical diagnoses to ICD-11 in Kananga,
  DR Congo
message: >-
  If you use this material, please cite the article once published, and this
  repository in the meantime.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Murhula Kabi
    given-names: Grâce
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0001-4386-1324
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Management Information Systems, Institut Supérieur de
      Commerce de Bukavu, Bukavu, DR Congo
    email: murhulakabi@iscbukavu.ac.cd
  - family-names: Ntaryamira
    given-names: Evariste
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Computer Science, Université Paris 8, France
abstract: >-
  Code, segmentation and matching rules, output schemas and aggregated results
  supporting a study on normalizing abbreviated French clinical diagnoses to
  the ICD-11 Mortality and Morbidity Statistics linearization, in a polyclinic
  in Kananga, Democratic Republic of the Congo. Corpus characterization,
  difficulty analysis and a reproducible lexical baseline. No individual-level
  data are distributed.
keywords:
  - ICD-11
  - concept normalization
  - clinical NLP
  - medical French
  - automated coding
  - low-resource settings
  - sub-Saharan Africa
license: MIT
